SIP attestation convention
================================================================================

The Starlight Intelligence Protocol (SIP) substrate documents in this
repository — including but not limited to SIP.md, SIS.md, ALLIANCE.md,
STACK.md, VOICES.md, VERTICALS.md, MEMORY.md, REGISTRY.md, SKILL.md, and
the substrate-tier commands under .claude/commands/ — are licensed under
MIT for maximum permissiveness.

As a social-layer convention (not a license restriction), forks,
derivatives, and downstream implementations are asked to preserve the
"Built on SIP" attestation in their artifacts when they compose with this
substrate. The attestation pattern is specified in SIP.md and the tooling
lives in /sip-attest. Silent composition is a breach of convention but not
of the MIT license.

This is the same shape used by Apache Foundation projects: LICENSE governs
legal rights; NOTICE captures attribution conventions that propagate with
forks.

